{
  "comment": "Ciena Waveserver 5 optical threshold notifications, transcribed from CIENA-WS-NOTIFICATION-MIB.mib (LAST-UPDATED 201611140000Z, Release 1.3) in the kcsinclair/mibs mirror. Ciena models an optical alarm as ONE notification type, wsLinkStateAlarmNotification (1.3.6.1.4.1.1271.3.2.12), whose varbinds carry the condition state -- NOT as a raise/clear pair of distinct traps like linkDown/linkUp. So all four entries share one trap OID and differ only in Severity (.7) and which condition flag is active. Flags are inactive(0)/active(1) per the MIB; a summary claiming active(2)/inactive(1) was wrong. Severity is non-contiguous: cleared(1) critical(3) major(4) minor(5) warning(6) info(8). The full flag list is emitted literally, as the real device does, so a collector parsing the whole varbind set sees the same shape it would in production. NOTE: because a clear zeroes every flag, the SD clear and the SF clear are identical on the wire apart from Description (.9) and Instance (.8). That is Ciena's model, not an omission here -- setting a condition flag on a clear would assert active(1) and cleared(1) at once. See ciena_waveserver5_limitations.md, 'A clear names its condition only in text'.",
